PATCH 172: STATEFUL ACCEPT-CASCADE DIAGNOSTIC HARNESS (env-gated FIST_CASCADE, DEFAULT OFF).

This is a DIAGNOSTIC harness, NOT a permanent flow-wiring (that is step 4, held until the cascade is
crash-free end-to-end).  It exists so future iterations stop rebuilding the throwaway ACCEPT-tail wiring
by hand: with FIST_CASCADE=1 in the environment, a REAL scripted-click route
    BATTLES(160,100) -> OK(205,128) -> ACCEPT(40,186)
runs the mission-start cascade instead of returning to the menu.  The three clicks establish the REAL
selected-battle state (cb7c->cc33 sets DGROUP:0xe834/0xe838 + the .FSG name), so the cascade runs with a
genuine mission selection -- a direct FUN_0000_e87a(0,0,0,0) probe does NOT work (cc33 stalls in the
FILEMGR .FSG enumeration because no battle is selected; documented probe artifact).

The inserted block is a FAITHFUL MIRROR of the pristine FUN_0000_e87a ACCEPT tail (re_out/fist.c
0xe89b..0xe929, lines 34124-34160): after the id=0 briefing modal FUN_0000_7088 returns with CF=0
(ACCEPT -- patch 154's cmp;cmc semantics, exposed here via the shim global g_fist_cf), it runs the
LOADING-screen setup + sim-reset + FSG parse + model-loader + display-list paint exactly as the pristine
e87a body does.  Concrete arg substitution for this dispatch context (the BATTLES state, param_1=param_3=
param_4=0): uVar1=high16(param_3)=0 -> uVar3=CONCAT22(0,8)=8; uVar4=0x4509; uVar6=0xf69; uVar2=0x157c;
the 459a seg arg=0x1c00; the filename ptr = &DAT_2000_39a9 (as pristine; 4754's real open uses the DOS
offset 0x79a9 directly per patch 156, so this ptr is faithful-but-unused-for-filename).

Because the whole block is gated behind getenv("FIST_CASCADE") (NULL by default), it is BEHAVIOUR-NEUTRAL
for the 19 verify flows (they never set FIST_CASCADE) -- verify.sh both stays 19/19, native<->wasm
bit-identical, no covered path changes.  getenv is available (ghidra_compat.h includes <stdlib.h>) and
portable to wasm (ENV mirrored via tools/wasm_pre.js).  Reproducible: run from the REPO ROOT with
    FIST_CASCADE=1 FIST_TICK_HZ=25000 FIST_RUNMS=<bounded> \
    FIST_MOUSE="200:160:100:0; 800:160:100:1; 1400:160:100:0; 3000:205:128:0; 3600:205:128:1; 4200:205:128:0; 5400:40:186:0; 6000:40:186:1; 6600:40:186:0" /tmp/fist_native

